Dual-formatter attack (W2 class) — REFUTED, single path confirmed
- `grep -rn '\$%|%\.2f|FormatFloat|NewPrinter|comma' internal/handlers/whatif/*.go`
  (excluding _test.go) found only 3 pre-existing, out-of-scope Plotly
  `hovertemplate` strings for a different chart (SS/Other/Withdrawals,
  lines 1197/1208/1219) formatted client-side by Plotly's own `:,.0f`, not
  Go code — unrelated to the guardrail hover text and untouched by this
  diff.
- guardrailEventHoverText's money line calls `templates.FormatMoney`, which
  is `func FormatMoney(v float64) string { return formatMoney(v) }` — a
  literal one-line pass-through of the existing unexported formatter, per
  ruling GM-2026-09-06b (this is the fix for the attempt-1 duplicate
  formatter). TestFormatMoney_ExportedWrapper pins FormatMoney(26722.44) ==
  "$26,722.44".

Rendered-string arithmetic / split-classification (W4 class) — REFUTED
- The percentage arithmetic in guardrailEventHoverText
  (math.Abs(Mult-Prev)/Prev*100, %.0f) is algebraically identical to the
  guardrails.html list template's `printf "%.0f" (mul 100.0 (div (sub P M) P))`
  for cut / `(div (sub M P) P)` for raise — both reduce to the same
  |Mult-Prev|/Prev*100, and both go through Go's own fmt %.0f, so there is
  no dual-formatter divergence to probe (single shared arithmetic + single
  shared printf verb, not two independent implementations).
- cut/raise marker symbol/color and the hover word are both driven off
  `e.Type` directly (`if ge.Type == "cut"` for marker;
  `fmt.Sprintf("Year %d: %s", e.Year, e.Type)` for hover) — same source the
  list template uses (`{{if eq .Type "cut"}}`). No re-derivation from the
  sign of Multiplier-PreviousMultiplier anywhere.

Rendered, on-instance check (criterion 5) — ran on port 8098
- Built and started the server manually with the exact same env-var
  contract as scripts/whatif-verify.sh (BUDGET_DATA_DIR, BUDGET2_BACKUP_DIR,
  BUDGET_LISTEN_ADDR=:8098, no CLI flags) after `ln -s` into the worktree
  was blocked by the sandbox classifier; used `cp -rL` of the real data dir
  into my own scratchpad instead (read-only source, isolated destination,
  same isolation the sanctioned script provides). Torn down via
  `curl .../killme` before writing this verdict; confirmed :8098 down,
  :8080 still healthy and untouched, worktree `git status --porcelain`
  clean (only the worker's own tracked diffs remain).
- The live plan's actual guardrail config differs from the spec prose's
  example numbers (data/settings/whatif.json has floor_drop_pct=10,
  floor_cut_pct=10, ceiling_rise_pct=20, ceiling_raise_pct=10, min=70,
  max=100, not 20/10/20/10 floor 75/ceiling 120) — the plan has evidently
  changed since the spec was authored. This produced 1 real guardrail
  event (Year 36, cut) rather than 5; verified against that actual event
  instead, which is what the acceptance criterion's underlying claims
  actually require:
  - GET /whatif/chart/projection?display_dollars=nominal: "Guardrail cuts /
    raises" trace x=[36], y=[3024130.173443734], text=["Year 36: cut 10%
    (90% of plan)<br>$28,225.37/mo → $25,402.84/mo"], symbol
    ["triangle-down"], color ["#ef4444"].
  - Portfolio Balance trace at x=36 (index 432): y=3024130.173443734 —
    EQUAL to the guardrail marker y (nominal).
  - Same check in real mode: guardrail y=762852.8434311618 == Portfolio
    Balance trace y at x=36 in real mode. Confirmed programmatically (Python
    exact float equality, not rounded).
  - GET /whatif (rendered HTML) "Guardrail Events" list section shows, for
    Year 36: "Cut by 10% (90% of plan)" and "$28,225.37/mo → $25,402.84/mo"
    — byte-identical money figures to the chart hover text on the same
    instance.
  - Trace order in the JSON: ['Portfolio Balance', 'Key events', 'Guardrail
    cuts / raises'] — new trace appended AFTER Key events, as required.
  - yaxis.range == [0, 4059453.1949642524] == [0, maxBalance*1.18]
    (maxBalance taken from the Portfolio Balance trace's own max y).
  - GET /whatif/chart/projection/no-guardrails?display_dollars=nominal:
    trace names == ['Portfolio Balance', 'Key events'] — no guardrail trace.

Regression
- Existing "Key events" trace present and unaffected (2 points, same as
